   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a product of \\( 5^{x} \\) and \\( \\sqrt{1 + \\sin(6x)} \\), so the product rule comes first: \\( f'(x) = \\left(5^{x}\\right)'\\,\\sqrt{1 + \\sin(6x)} + 5^{x}\\left(\\sqrt{1 + \\sin(6x)}\\right)' \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               5,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Sqrt",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Sin",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        6,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ],
                  1
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 5^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 5^{x} \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               5,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               5
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Write the root as the power \\( \\left(1 + \\sin(6x)\\right)^{1/2} \\) so the power rule applies to the outer layer. The factor \\( \\sqrt{1 + \\sin(6x)} \\) is a square root of \\( 1 + \\sin(6x) \\), which contains a sine of \\( 6x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(\\sqrt{1 + \\sin(6x)}\\right)' = \\frac{3 \\cos{\\left(6 x \\right)}}{\\sqrt{\\sin{\\left(6 x \\right)} + 1}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               3,
               [
                  "Cos",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     6,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Sqrt",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Sin",
                     [
                        "Multiply",
                        6,
                        "x"
                     ]
                  ],
                  1
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Assemble the product rule and evaluate at \\( x = 0 \\): \\( f'(0) = \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} + 3 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Ln",
               5
            ],
            3
         ]
      }
